# OpenLeet Environment Configuration Template
# Copy this file to .env and adjust values for your environment.
#
# ZERO-TRUST CLIENT:
# - No Firebase service account JSON is used or accepted by this build.
# - FIREBASE_API_KEY is a public client identifier, not an admin credential.
# - The signed-in user's ID token is kept in memory and sent directly to
#   Firestore. Firestore Security Rules must restrict users/{uid} to
#   request.auth.uid == uid and leaderboard/{uid} to the matching writer.
#   See firestore.rules.
# - The local profile is encrypted with a key derived from the current OS user,
#   so it is readable offline and unique per machine account.
#
# Settings -> ACCOUNT reads FIREBASE_API_KEY from the process environment or a
# .env in the user config directory / current directory. PROJECT_ID and
# LOCAL_SAVE_FILE_PATH are required only for cloud profile sync.
#
# Google browser sign-in is optional. In Google Cloud Console open
# Google Auth Platform -> Clients (older consoles: APIs & Services ->
# Credentials), create an OAuth client of type "Desktop app" in the same
# project as Firebase, then paste the client ID and client secret below.
# Desktop client secrets are not confidential; PKCE and a loopback redirect
# are still used, and no redirect URI needs to be registered.
#
# These Firebase web-app values are SDK metadata and are not read by the
# current Go REST client. They are kept here for reference only:
# FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=your-project.firebaseapp.com
# FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=your-project.firebasestorage.app
# FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=000000000000
# FIREBASE_APP_ID=1:000000000000:web:0000000000000000000000
# FIREBASE_MEASUREMENT_ID=G-XXXXXXXXXX
#
# FIREBASE_APP_ID is only used by Firebase SDKs. This build talks to the
# Identity Toolkit and Firestore REST APIs, so it needs FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID
# and FIREBASE_API_KEY below.
#
# Never commit your real .env. FIREBASE_API_KEY is a public client identifier,
# but it belongs to your own Firebase project; use your own values.
#
# Relative paths resolve from the current process working directory.

FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=your-firebase-project-id
FIREBASE_API_KEY=your-firebase-web-api-key
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=
GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=
LOCAL_SAVE_FILE_PATH=./openleet_data.enc
